      en: "The Bodu Thakurufaanu Memorial Center in Malé commemorates the national hero Bodu Thakurufaanu, who led the resistance against Portuguese colonization in the 16th century. It serves as a museum and cultural hub, showcasing artifacts, documents, and interactive exhibits about Maldivian independence. The building, opened in 2006, features a blend of traditional Maldivian architecture and modern design. The center hosts educational programs, attracting over 20,000 visitors annually. It stands as a symbol of national pride and historical preservation. The memorial is located near the Islamic Centre and is a key stop for tourists interested in Maldivian history.",
